{"title":"Mathematical Data and Constants","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":"Mathematical Data and Constants","author":"Sugeng Riyanto, M.Sc.","date":"2026","format":{"pdf":{"toc":false},"html":{"toc":true}}},"headingText":"Physical Constants","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\n\n| Constant | Symbol | Value |\n|:---------|:-------|:------|\n| Speed of light in vacuum | $c$ | $3.0 \\times 10^8 \\text{ m/s}$ |\n| Acceleration of free fall | $g$ | $9.8 \\text{ m/s}^2$ (or $10 \\text{ m/s}^2$) |\n| Hubble constant | $H_0$ | $2.2 \\times 10^{-18} \\text{ s}^{-1}$ |\n| 1 light-year | ly | $9.5 \\times 10^{15} \\text{ m}$ |\n| Absolute zero | | $-273°\\text{C}$ or $0 \\text{ K}$ |\n\n---\n\n## SI Unit Prefixes\n\n| Prefix | Symbol | Factor |\n|:-------|:-------|:-------|\n| giga- | G | $10^9$ |\n| mega- | M | $10^6$ |\n| kilo- | k | $10^3$ |\n| centi- | c | $10^{-2}$ |\n| milli- | m | $10^{-3}$ |\n| micro- | μ | $10^{-6}$ |\n| nano- | n | $10^{-9}$ |\n\n---\n\n## Densities of Common Materials\n\n| Material | Density (kg/m³) | Density (g/cm³) |\n|:---------|:----------------|:----------------|\n| Air | 1.2 | 0.0012 |\n| Water | 1000 | 1.0 |\n| Seawater | 1025 | 1.025 |\n| Ice | 917 | 0.917 |\n| Aluminium | 2700 | 2.7 |\n| Iron/Steel | 7800 | 7.8 |\n| Copper | 8900 | 8.9 |\n| Lead | 11300 | 11.3 |\n| Gold | 19300 | 19.3 |\n\n---\n\n## Specific Heat Capacities\n\n| Material | Specific Heat Capacity (J/kg·K) |\n|:---------|:-------------------------------|\n| Water | 4200 |\n| Seawater | 3900 |\n| Ice | 2100 |\n| Aluminium | 900 |\n| Iron | 460 |\n| Copper | 400 |\n| Lead | 130 |\n\n---\n\n## Electromagnetic Spectrum\n\n| Region | Wavelength Range | Frequency Range |\n|:-------|:-----------------|:----------------|\n| Radio waves | > 0.1 m | < 3 × 10⁹ Hz |\n| Microwaves | 10⁻³ – 0.1 m | 3 × 10⁹ – 3 × 10¹¹ Hz |\n| Infrared | 7 × 10⁻⁷ – 10⁻³ m | 3 × 10¹¹ – 4 × 10¹⁴ Hz |\n| Visible light | 4 × 10⁻⁷ – 7 × 10⁻⁷ m | 4 × 10¹⁴ – 7.5 × 10¹⁴ Hz |\n| Ultraviolet | 10⁻⁸ – 4 × 10⁻⁷ m | 7.5 × 10¹⁴ – 3 × 10¹⁶ Hz |\n| X-rays | 10⁻¹¹ – 10⁻⁸ m | 3 × 10¹⁶ – 3 × 10¹⁹ Hz |\n| Gamma rays | < 10⁻¹¹ m | > 3 × 10¹⁹ Hz |\n\n---\n\n## Mathematical Formulae\n\n### Geometry\n- Circumference of circle: $C = 2\\pi r = \\pi d$\n- Area of rectangle: $A = lw$\n- Area of triangle: $A = \\frac{1}{2}bh$\n- Area of circle: $A = \\pi r^2$\n- Volume of rectangular block: $V = lwh$\n- Volume of cylinder: $V = \\pi r^2h$\n- Volume of sphere: $V = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3$\n\n### Trigonometry\n- Pythagoras' theorem: $a^2 + b^2 = c^2$\n- $\\sin \\theta = \\frac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n- $\\cos \\theta = \\frac{\\text{adjacent}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n- $\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{adjacent}}$\n\n### Standard Form\n- Numbers written as $A \\times 10^n$ where $1 \\leq A < 10$","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\n## Physical Constants\n\n| Constant | Symbol | Value |\n|:---------|:-------|:------|\n| Speed of light in vacuum | $c$ | $3.0 \\times 10^8 \\text{ m/s}$ |\n| Acceleration of free fall | $g$ | $9.8 \\text{ m/s}^2$ (or $10 \\text{ m/s}^2$) |\n| Hubble constant | $H_0$ | $2.2 \\times 10^{-18} \\text{ s}^{-1}$ |\n| 1 light-year | ly | $9.5 \\times 10^{15} \\text{ m}$ |\n| Absolute zero | | $-273°\\text{C}$ or $0 \\text{ K}$ |\n\n---\n\n## SI Unit Prefixes\n\n| Prefix | Symbol | Factor |\n|:-------|:-------|:-------|\n| giga- | G | $10^9$ |\n| mega- | M | $10^6$ |\n| kilo- | k | $10^3$ |\n| centi- | c | $10^{-2}$ |\n| milli- | m | $10^{-3}$ |\n| micro- | μ | $10^{-6}$ |\n| nano- | n | $10^{-9}$ |\n\n---\n\n## Densities of Common Materials\n\n| Material | Density (kg/m³) | Density (g/cm³) |\n|:---------|:----------------|:----------------|\n| Air | 1.2 | 0.0012 |\n| Water | 1000 | 1.0 |\n| Seawater | 1025 | 1.025 |\n| Ice | 917 | 0.917 |\n| Aluminium | 2700 | 2.7 |\n| Iron/Steel | 7800 | 7.8 |\n| Copper | 8900 | 8.9 |\n| Lead | 11300 | 11.3 |\n| Gold | 19300 | 19.3 |\n\n---\n\n## Specific Heat Capacities\n\n| Material | Specific Heat Capacity (J/kg·K) |\n|:------